# Seat probe P1 — scratch Windows-only CI run 39355882657 (draft pull request #88, branch seatmut/wwcr-p1 at 97eb8a81, main 27fb9d3c's code), 2026-10-20 UTC

Result: step 1 printed 1,5 and a comma CPU value under an in-process de-DE thread culture in Windows PowerShell 5.1.26100 (and in pwsh 7), so the plan's decision is: build as written. After Set-Culture de-DE, a new powershell process printed de-DE and CPU 0,5 (ticks 5000000). Step 4: main's win32-launch.test.mjs failed 'Windows: a busy pi is not stopped as stalled' under de-DE, with cpu=0s reads and STALL. Step 3b used bash's own pid, which is not a Windows pid, so its not-found error says nothing about the read. The full job log follows.

